;M600 for the TWP config (lcnc-suite, 2026-09-04): the bundled
; tool_length_probe/m600.ngc runs tool_touch_off, which retracts and
; positions with G53. Under switched kinematics G53 addresses the
; kinematics' WORLD frame (the tilted plane frame in TOOL mode, the
; table-riding frame in TCP), so the toolsetter moves land in the wrong
; place. This wrapper shadows the bundle's (first on SUBROUTINE_PATH):
; save the switchkins type, force identity (M428), measure, restore
; (M430 re-selects G59, M429 TCP). Under task the HAL pin is the truth;
; the preview parse has no HAL and reads the interpreter mirror
; #<_webui_kinstype> every switch site maintains — so the preview restores
; the same type the machine will (a type-2 span after the change keeps
; the plane frame the last G53.x pinned). Identity in → identity out:
; nothing changes for the common case (the UI only offers Measure / Load
; in the Machine frame — machineFrame gate; this covers a PROGRAM's M6/
; M600 while tilted).
o<m600> sub
(WEBUI_SUB=m600) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker, silent in task
#<saved_kins> = 0
o100 if [EXISTS[#<_webui_kinstype>]]
  #<saved_kins> = #<_webui_kinstype>
o100 endif
o110 if [#<_task> EQ 1]
o111   if [EXISTS[#<_hal[motion.switchkins-type]>]]
         #<saved_kins> = #<_hal[motion.switchkins-type]>
o111   endif
o110 endif
o120 if [#<saved_kins> NE 0]
  M428                      ; identity kinematics for the G53 moves (marker + mirror inside)
o120 endif
#2000 = 1
o<tool_touch_off> call
o130 if [#<saved_kins> EQ 2]
  M430                      ; TOOL kinematics + G59 again (the plane frame is still pinned)
o130 elseif [#<saved_kins> EQ 1]
  M429                      ; TCP again
o130 endif
(WEBUI_SUB_END) ;lcnc-suite: preview sub-span marker
o<m600> endsub
M2 (end program)
